       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the IR maximum. Even a single 1,700 mg dose is above the usual per-dose range of 500\u20131,000 mg. Overdosing on metformin raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and the patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
